\section{Proposed Future-Aware PPO Agent}
\label{sec:method}

In this section, we present the architecture of our Lyapunov-Guided Future-Aware PPO agent. The system comprises three key modules: (1) The Future-Aware State Space construction, (2) The Neural Network Architecture (Actor-Critic), and (3) The Lyapunov-Regularized Reward Mechanism.

\subsection{Future-Aware State Space}
Unlike standard ABR agents (e.g., Pensieve) that rely solely on historical observations, our agent explicitly observes the immediate future characteristics of the video. The state vector at time $t$, denoted as $s_t$, is defined as:
\begin{equation}
    s_t = \{ \vec{x}_t, \vec{\tau}_t, \vec{n}_t, b_t, f_{next}, v_{next} \}
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\vec{x}_t$: Vector of the past $k=8$ throughput measurements.
    \item $\vec{\tau}_t$: Vector of the past $k=8$ download times.
    \item $\vec{n}_t$: Vector of the past $k=8$ selected chunk sizes.
    \item $b_t$: Current buffer occupancy (in seconds).
    \item $f_{next}$: \textbf{(Novelty)} The exact file sizes of the next chunk at all available bitrates (e.g., sizes for 360p, 720p, 1080p...). This helps the agent avoid selecting a high bitrate if the specific chunk is unusually large (complex scene).
    \item $v_{next}$: The VMAF scores of the next chunk for all bitrates, enabling content-aware decisions.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Network Architecture}
We employ an Actor-Critic architecture based on Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO). 
The input features are processed through two separate branches:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{1D-CNN Branch:} The time-series inputs ($\vec{x}_t, \vec{\tau}_t$) are passed through a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (128 filters, kernel size 4) to extract temporal network patterns.
    \item \textbf{MLP Branch:} The scalar and vector inputs ($b_t, f_{next}$) are processed via a fully connected layer.
\end{itemize}
The outputs of these branches are concatenated and fed into the shared hidden layers (two layers of 128 units with Tanh activation). Finally, the network splits into:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Actor Head:} Outputs a probability distribution $\pi(a|s)$ over the discrete bitrate actions using a Softmax layer.
    \item \textbf{Critic Head:} Outputs the estimated value function $V(s)$ used to compute the advantage function.
\end{enumerate}

